 "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tAmharic Gemination Lexicon v3\n\t\n\nWhich consonants are doubled in each of 86,022 Amharic words, for every reading\nof the word, and where each doubling comes from. Built by Dataset.ET with the\nHornMorpho morphological analyzer, corrected with rules that native listening,\nArmbruster's hand-marked verb tables and recorded speech agree on.\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\nWord types\n86,022 (856,734 corpus tokens)\n\n\nAnalyzed by HornMorpho\n56,964 types, 84.0% of tokens\n\n\nWords with a geminate in the top… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Chapimenge/amharic-gemination-lexicon.",
